  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "SSLClientHelloMessage",
    "file": "PcapPlusPlus/Packet++/src/SSLHandshake.cpp",
    "description": "In SSLClientHelloMessage::SSLClientHelloMessage(), extension parsing trusts computed offsets/lengths derived from attacker-controlled ClientHello fields (session ID length, cipher suite count/length, compression methods, extensions length) without validating that curPos actually points inside m_Data before dereferencing *(uint16_t*)curPos. The loop condition uses messageLen/extensionLength bookkeeping, but does not guarantee extensionPos<=m_Data+messageLen or that each extension header is fully in-bounds before read, leading to OOB read at line ~1320.",
    "conditions": "FuzzTarget feeds crafted packet bytes into Packet/Tcp/SSL parsing. Input must be recognized as SSL handshake and as CLIENT_HELLO; then malformed internal length fields in ClientHello must make extensionLengthOffset/extensionPos and subsequent curPos advancement inconsistent with actual captured buffer size (or with true message boundaries). When constructor enters extension loop, it performs 2-byte read of extension type from curPos beyond allocated packet buffer, triggering ASan heap-buffer-overflow."
  },
